# Generated from the Python Pydantic models by `pnpm schema:generate`, and
# checked for drift by `pnpm schema:check` — which compares the file on disk
# against what the generator emits, byte for byte. Prettier rewrapping a union
# it emitted one-member-per-line is therefore a *failing build*, not a tidy-up:
# two gateway tests read that check and both went red the first time a
# `--write` pass reached these three files. One entry here rather than an
# `exclude` on the pre-commit hook, because Prettier honours this file for
# paths named on the command line too — so it also covers the package's own
# `format` script and any hand-run `pnpm exec prettier`.
